1
00:01:35,479 --> 00:01:36,039
Master,

2
00:01:36,039 --> 00:01:37,080
please calm down.

3
00:01:38,160 --> 00:01:38,960
This Siberian tiger,

4
00:01:38,960 --> 00:01:41,640
no, this Dong Beihu,

5
00:01:41,880 --> 00:01:43,960
is the son of Lawyer Xiao's current landlord.

6
00:01:43,960 --> 00:01:46,090
He helps bring in cases at her law firm.

7
00:01:46,280 --> 00:01:48,800
He has a rather quirky personality.

8
00:01:48,920 --> 00:01:49,759
Absurd.

9
00:01:50,640 --> 00:01:52,570
She wants to make a name for herself

10
00:01:52,600 --> 00:01:54,800
with a team like this?

11
00:01:55,920 --> 00:01:58,180
In the future, for these minor disputes,

12
00:01:58,479 --> 00:02:00,680
just hand them over to the team lawyers.

13
00:02:00,960 --> 00:02:03,490
Don't let them take up too much of your energy.

14
00:02:03,720 --> 00:02:04,800
Tell me, this Xiao Longnv,

15
00:02:04,800 --> 00:02:07,400
where did she gather this bunch of 'geniuses'?

16
00:02:07,720 --> 00:02:10,720
A living bean bun, all greasy.

17
00:02:11,120 --> 00:02:12,520
One following her around,

18
00:02:12,520 --> 00:02:14,050
a bouncing little pumpkin.

19
00:02:14,160 --> 00:02:15,480
And there's an even better one,

20
00:02:15,480 --> 00:02:18,160
acting like a hooligan and stealing rice crusts.

21
00:02:18,160 --> 00:02:19,800
Stop talking nonsense.

22
00:02:20,040 --> 00:02:22,700
You're the one chattering the most all day long.

23
00:02:23,320 --> 00:02:25,520
Just tell me if what I said is true or not.

24
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:26,480
If Xiao Longnv got these guys

25
00:02:26,480 --> 00:02:28,360
from blind boxes,

26
00:02:29,040 --> 00:02:30,300
she's really unlucky.

27
00:02:30,800 --> 00:02:32,460
Speaking of being unlucky...

28
00:02:32,520 --> 00:02:33,780
Our leader is the best.

29
00:02:34,600 --> 00:02:35,320
Why?

30
00:02:35,760 --> 00:02:36,880
He brought you out.

31
00:02:39,160 --> 00:02:40,040
Annoying.

32
00:02:41,680 --> 00:02:44,240
Here, your favorite potato and bean stew.

33
00:02:44,240 --> 00:02:45,160
Thanks, Mom.

34
00:02:50,320 --> 00:02:52,040
How's Jiayi's matter going?

35
00:02:52,160 --> 00:02:54,760
Which lawyer from your firm did you introduce?

36
00:02:55,040 --> 00:02:57,040
Li Xin, Lawyer Li.

37
00:02:57,320 --> 00:02:58,600
He happens to be

38
00:02:58,600 --> 00:03:00,960
the legal advisor for Jiayi's airline.

39
00:03:00,960 --> 00:03:03,420
So he can handle this for Jiayi along the way.

40
00:03:03,760 --> 00:03:04,520
Li Xin.

41
00:03:05,520 --> 00:03:07,780
I think I've heard you mention that name.

42
00:03:08,680 --> 00:03:10,320
Is he the one who's really impressive?

43
00:03:10,320 --> 00:03:11,650
He's super impressive.

44
00:03:12,160 --> 00:03:14,680
He's the youngest senior partner at Honghu.

45
00:03:17,320 --> 00:03:18,520
Young and promising.

46
00:03:18,600 --> 00:03:20,400
You should learn from him.

47
00:03:22,320 --> 00:03:23,680
How can I learn from him?

48
00:03:23,960 --> 00:03:24,760
He's a lawyer.

49
00:03:24,760 --> 00:03:25,520
I'm in admin.

50
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:26,980
We have nothing in common.

51
00:03:27,040 --> 00:03:28,240
You lack ambition.

52
00:03:28,960 --> 00:03:31,320
You're already on such a good platform.

53
00:03:31,320 --> 00:03:33,680
Why don't you think about moving up?

54
00:03:35,320 --> 00:03:37,120
Go take the bar exam.

55
00:03:37,480 --> 00:03:39,880
Once you pass, ask Lawyer Li to mentor you.

56
00:03:40,320 --> 00:03:41,840
Your dad's suggestion is good.

57
00:03:41,840 --> 00:03:43,640
I'll sign you up for a bar exam prep class.

58
00:03:43,640 --> 00:03:45,640
You two make it sound so easy.

59
00:03:45,760 --> 00:03:47,200
The bar exam is super hard.

60
00:03:47,200 --> 00:03:48,880
There's an intern at our law firm

61
00:03:48,880 --> 00:03:50,810
who hasn't passed it in five years.

62
00:03:52,160 --> 00:03:53,320
Even Honghu has interns

63
00:03:53,320 --> 00:03:55,600
who can't pass the bar exam?

64
00:03:59,160 --> 00:03:59,880
Of course.

65
00:04:00,560 --> 00:04:05,040
He's the nephew of the head of the marketing department.

66
00:04:05,320 --> 00:04:07,450
He got in purely through connections.

67
00:04:07,760 --> 00:04:08,880
It's a society of connections.

68
00:04:08,880 --> 00:04:11,160
See? You still have to rely on connections.

69
00:04:11,160 --> 00:04:12,000
Miaomiao,

70
00:04:12,040 --> 00:04:13,160
let me tell you.

71
00:04:13,320 --> 00:04:14,760
You need to be smart about things.

72
00:04:14,760 --> 00:04:17,480
You have to build a good relationship with your boss, you know?

73
00:04:17,480 --> 00:04:18,279
I know.

74
00:04:18,600 --> 00:04:19,480
Let's eat.

75
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:20,640
Come eat.

76
00:04:30,480 --> 00:04:31,280
Ouch.

77
00:04:31,280 --> 00:04:32,360
Are you scrubbing a steel plate?

78
00:04:32,360 --> 00:04:33,159
Does it hurt?

79
00:04:33,159 --> 00:04:34,200
Of course it does.

80
00:04:38,480 --> 00:04:39,080
It hurts.

81
00:04:39,320 --> 00:04:40,850
Will you remember the pain?

82
00:04:41,040 --> 00:04:42,159
What are you doing? Are you lecturing me?

83
00:04:42,159 --> 00:04:43,920
Why are you so arrogant?

84
00:04:43,920 --> 00:04:44,920
I find you a bit...

85
00:04:45,720 --> 00:04:47,600
Uncle, I just joined the law firm.

86
00:04:48,159 --> 00:04:49,920
If you cause any more trouble,

87
00:04:50,320 --> 00:04:52,720
Director Xiao will get mad and kick me out.

88
00:04:52,920 --> 00:04:53,920
Kick you out?

89
00:04:54,040 --> 00:04:55,200
We are on the same level, you know?

90
00:04:55,200 --> 00:04:56,159
We are equals.

91
00:04:56,159 --> 00:04:57,200
Who's kicking who?

92
00:04:57,200 --> 00:04:58,320
Be humble.

93
00:04:58,720 --> 00:04:59,720
It hurts, Luo Zhi.

94
00:05:06,920 --> 00:05:07,760
It's about time.

95
00:05:07,760 --> 00:05:08,620
Get ready to go.

96
00:05:09,360 --> 00:05:11,000
If the reconciliation goes smoothly today,

97
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:12,860
Jiayi will finally find closure.

98
00:05:13,360 --> 00:05:16,920
Remember, don't provoke her today.

99
00:05:17,040 --> 00:05:18,320
Make sure everything goes smoothly.

100
00:05:18,320 --> 00:05:19,250
Especially you.

101
00:05:19,320 --> 00:05:20,880
You just drive.

102
00:05:20,880 --> 00:05:22,040
Don't talk nonsense.

103
00:05:22,040 --> 00:05:24,000
Don't wander off, and don't mess up.

104
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:25,000
Can you do that?

105
00:05:31,040 --> 00:05:31,880
Jiayi.

106
00:05:32,840 --> 00:05:33,760
Hello, Jiayi.

107
00:05:34,480 --> 00:05:36,140
We are on our way to pick you up.

108
00:05:36,200 --> 00:05:37,440
Sorry, Miaomiao.

109
00:05:38,159 --> 00:05:40,000
I'm really not feeling well.

110
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:42,330
I might need to rest a bit before going out.

111
00:05:44,440 --> 00:05:45,760
It's okay, Jiayi.

112
00:05:45,880 --> 00:05:47,960
Take your time. Leave when you feel better.

113
00:05:47,960 --> 00:05:48,960
No rush.

114
00:05:49,320 --> 00:05:50,520
Thank you, Ms. Xiao.

115
00:05:50,760 --> 00:05:52,040
Sorry for the trouble.

116
00:05:56,320 --> 00:05:57,780
Alright, change of plans.

117
00:05:58,080 --> 00:05:59,600
I'll go to the airline first.

118
00:05:59,600 --> 00:06:00,800
You two go pick her up.

119
00:06:01,200 --> 00:06:02,960
Remember, don't agitate her.

120
00:06:02,960 --> 00:06:04,200
Be mindful of her feelings.

121
00:06:04,200 --> 00:06:05,060
Can you do that?

122
00:06:05,400 --> 00:06:06,080
Promise?

123
00:06:06,080 --> 00:06:06,760
Understood.

124
00:06:06,760 --> 00:06:07,400
Okay.

125
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:09,720
Director, can I go with them?

126
00:06:11,960 --> 00:06:12,520
Okay.

127
00:06:15,200 --> 00:06:17,080
Why are you joining the fun?

128
00:06:17,320 --> 00:06:18,720
I'll go keep an eye on things for you.

129
00:06:18,720 --> 00:06:19,840
Keep an eye on what?

130
00:06:20,320 --> 00:06:21,200
On you.

131
00:06:21,200 --> 00:06:22,320
Are you crazy?

132
00:06:22,880 --> 00:06:24,010
Should be here soon.

133
00:06:25,960 --> 00:06:26,840
Hello, Attorney Xiao.

134
00:06:26,840 --> 00:06:27,200
Nice to meet you.

135
00:06:27,200 --> 00:06:28,040
Hello, Attorney Xiao.

136
00:06:28,040 --> 00:06:28,520
Hello.

137
00:06:28,880 --> 00:06:29,940
Please have a seat.

138
00:06:30,040 --> 00:06:31,200
Hello, Mr. Hu.

139
00:06:31,400 --> 00:06:33,840
I am Xu Jiayi's attorney, Xiao Longnv.

140
00:06:37,880 --> 00:06:38,640
Hello.

141
00:06:38,640 --> 00:06:40,400
I'm Mr. Hu's attorney.

142
00:06:40,400 --> 00:06:41,400
I'm Wu Yong.

143
00:06:41,400 --> 00:06:43,130
Hello, Mr. Wu. Nice to meet you.

144
00:06:44,640 --> 00:06:45,440
Are you alone?

145
00:06:45,640 --> 00:06:46,570
She didn't come?

146
00:06:46,640 --> 00:06:47,520
Doesn't she want me to apologize?

147
00:06:47,520 --> 00:06:48,080
She's coming.

148
00:06:48,080 --> 00:06:50,159
She felt a little unwell on the way.

149
00:06:50,159 --> 00:06:51,520
My colleague went to pick her up.

150
00:06:51,520 --> 00:06:52,760
In the meantime,

151
00:06:52,760 --> 00:06:54,159
I'd like to talk to Mr. Hu

152
00:06:54,159 --> 00:06:55,820
about her current condition.

153
00:06:56,040 --> 00:06:56,570
Go ahead.

154
00:06:59,840 --> 00:07:02,480
Jiayi, are you okay?

155
00:07:02,840 --> 00:07:03,840
Much better.

156
00:07:07,040 --> 00:07:08,840
I need to take a call. Wait for me.

157
00:07:09,520 --> 00:07:11,640
Hurry up.

158
00:07:14,080 --> 00:07:14,880
Hello, Mom.

159
00:07:14,880 --> 00:07:15,520
What's up?

160
00:07:15,720 --> 00:07:17,480
Miaomiao, what are you doing?

161
00:07:17,880 --> 00:07:19,520
I'm at work. What's wrong?

162
00:07:19,840 --> 00:07:20,770
That's perfect.

163
00:07:20,840 --> 00:07:23,700
Your dad and I are right downstairs at your law firm.

164
00:07:24,200 --> 00:07:26,400
What? You two came to Honghu?

165
00:07:26,400 --> 00:07:28,200
Miaomiao, come down right now.

166
00:07:28,520 --> 00:07:29,400
I'll tell you when you get down here.

167
00:07:29,400 --> 00:07:30,160
Okay.

168
00:07:30,160 --> 00:07:31,840
Stay right there and wait for me.

169
00:07:31,840 --> 00:07:33,520
I'm coming down right now.

170
00:07:38,080 --> 00:07:39,840
You've got some nerve.

171
00:07:40,520 --> 00:07:42,040
Does the director know about this?

172
00:07:42,040 --> 00:07:43,640
No, he doesn't.

173
00:07:44,200 --> 00:07:45,720
I don't have time to explain it to you two right now.

174
00:07:45,720 --> 00:07:46,880
Please keep it a secret for me, okay?

175
00:07:46,880 --> 00:07:47,840
I'm begging you.

176
00:07:47,840 --> 00:07:49,400
Then you owe us a big favor.

177
00:07:49,400 --> 00:07:50,880
Okay, bro. I'll owe you whatever.

178
00:07:50,880 --> 00:07:51,520
You two must

179
00:07:51,520 --> 00:07:53,640
get Jiayi safely to the airline.

180
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:54,640
Thank you.

181
00:07:54,840 --> 00:07:56,300
Let me have a word with her.

182
00:07:56,520 --> 00:07:58,640
Little girl, you're two-faced.

183
00:07:59,640 --> 00:08:02,570
You can never keep secrets from your uncle, you know?

184
00:08:06,640 --> 00:08:07,840
They haven't arrived yet.

185
00:08:07,840 --> 00:08:09,520
I've wasted my whole morning here.

186
00:08:09,520 --> 00:08:11,520
They are on their way, Mr. Hu.

187
00:08:11,520 --> 00:08:12,640
It's mainly because Xu Jiayi

188
00:08:12,640 --> 00:08:14,200
hasn't been in a good state recently.

189
00:08:14,200 --> 00:08:16,400
Going out, meeting people,

190
00:08:16,400 --> 00:08:17,520
especially strangers,

191
00:08:17,520 --> 00:08:18,960
and taking public transportation,

192
00:08:18,960 --> 00:08:20,760
all put her under a lot of psychological pressure.

193
00:08:20,760 --> 00:08:22,520
Mr. Hu, please understand.

194
00:08:22,640 --> 00:08:24,200
Let's face the problem together

195
00:08:24,200 --> 00:08:25,460
and solve it together.

196
00:08:25,640 --> 00:08:27,840
Yes, let's stay calm.

197
00:08:28,080 --> 00:08:29,640
Mr. Hu, please bear with us.

198
00:08:29,720 --> 00:08:31,040
My time is also very precious.

199
00:08:31,040 --> 00:08:31,960
An hour of my time is not cheaper

200
00:08:31,960 --> 00:08:32,960
than these lawyers.

201
00:08:32,960 --> 00:08:33,280
Yes.

202
00:08:33,280 --> 00:08:35,200
Who will compensate me for delaying my business?

203
00:08:35,200 --> 00:08:36,080
Yes, yes.

204
00:08:55,400 --> 00:08:56,200
Uncle, uncle.

205
00:09:00,280 --> 00:09:01,480
Uncle, turn here.

206
00:09:01,480 --> 00:09:03,610
There's a shortcut here. Hurry, turn.

207
00:09:11,960 --> 00:09:13,160
Why hasn't he come down yet?

208
00:09:13,160 --> 00:09:15,640
Exactly. What is this kid doing?

209
00:09:15,880 --> 00:09:17,080
It's been so long.

210
00:09:33,600 --> 00:09:34,640
Do you know where she is?

211
00:09:34,640 --> 00:09:35,840
Mom, Dad.

212
00:09:38,080 --> 00:09:38,280
Miaomiao.

213
00:09:38,280 --> 00:09:38,880
What's wrong?

214
00:09:38,880 --> 00:09:39,400
Sweetie.

215
00:09:39,400 --> 00:09:40,640
What happened to you?

216
00:09:40,640 --> 00:09:41,760
You're sweating all over.

217
00:09:41,760 --> 00:09:42,820
You're all sweaty.

218
00:09:43,160 --> 00:09:45,040
I was rushing up and down delivering documents.

219
00:09:45,040 --> 00:09:45,720
What is it?

220
00:09:45,720 --> 00:09:47,720
Your mom and I were shopping nearby.

221
00:09:47,760 --> 00:09:49,960
So we bought some things to bring to you.

222
00:09:50,280 --> 00:09:51,080
Later.

223
00:09:51,080 --> 00:09:54,080
Take this up to Lawyer Li.

224
00:09:54,400 --> 00:09:55,640
Why give it to Lawyer Li?

225
00:09:55,640 --> 00:09:57,200
To build a good relationship.

226
00:09:57,200 --> 00:09:59,480
It's all about social etiquette, sweetie.

227
00:09:59,480 --> 00:10:01,040
You really are my own parents.

228
00:10:01,040 --> 00:10:03,170
Yes. Remember, you must give it to him.

229
00:10:05,440 --> 00:10:06,800
My colleague is looking for me. Hurry.

230
00:10:06,800 --> 00:10:07,440
Go back. Okay.

231
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:08,120
We're leaving then.

232
00:10:08,120 --> 00:10:08,720
Go.

233
00:10:08,720 --> 00:10:10,000
Make sure you remember what I taught you.

234
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:10,560
I know.

235
00:10:10,560 --> 00:10:11,080
Hurry.

236
00:10:15,080 --> 00:10:16,360
Uncle, no, that's not right.

237
00:10:16,360 --> 00:10:17,480
I think the navigation is wrong.

238
00:10:17,480 --> 00:10:18,720
What the hell? Look.

239
00:10:26,080 --> 00:10:27,200
How do you drive?

240
00:10:27,200 --> 00:10:28,480
You crashed into my new car.

241
00:10:28,480 --> 00:10:30,120
Sorry, bro. I have an emergency.

242
00:10:30,120 --> 00:10:31,200
How about this? I'll leave you my number.

243
00:10:31,200 --> 00:10:32,760
I'll contact you later, okay?

244
00:10:32,760 --> 00:10:34,000
What do you mean? Are you trying to run away?

245
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:35,120
No, I'm really not.

246
00:10:35,120 --> 00:10:36,240
No, bro, listen to me. I'm getting out.

247
00:10:36,240 --> 00:10:36,920
Get out of the car.

248
00:10:36,920 --> 00:10:38,680
I know, I know. I'm getting out.

249
00:10:38,680 --> 00:10:39,560
Don't... Don't knock.

250
00:10:39,560 --> 00:10:40,680
Stop making noise.

251
00:10:40,680 --> 00:10:41,600
Don't hit it. It's fine.

252
00:10:41,600 --> 00:10:42,480
Jiayi, it's fine.

253
00:10:42,480 --> 00:10:42,960
Get out of the car.

254
00:10:42,960 --> 00:10:44,120
Stop hitting it.

255
00:10:44,360 --> 00:10:45,200
Get out.

256
00:10:45,240 --> 00:10:46,360
Get out of the car. Get out now.

257
00:10:46,360 --> 00:10:47,440
Get out. Get out.

258
00:10:47,440 --> 00:10:48,120
Stop knocking.

259
00:10:48,120 --> 00:10:49,600
Stop yelling. I'm getting out.

260
00:10:49,600 --> 00:10:50,860
I'm getting out, okay?

261
00:10:51,440 --> 00:10:52,200
I'm in a hurry to get to the hospital.

262
00:10:52,200 --> 00:10:53,360
Otherwise, I wouldn't be in such a rush.

263
00:10:53,360 --> 00:10:54,120
Jiayi.

264
00:10:54,760 --> 00:10:56,640
Uncle, Jiayi fainted.

265
00:10:56,840 --> 00:10:58,240
What did you do?

266
00:11:00,320 --> 00:11:01,600
Alright, I got it.

267
00:11:05,320 --> 00:11:06,320
I'm sorry, everyone.

268
00:11:06,320 --> 00:11:07,840
On her way here, Xu Jiayi

269
00:11:07,840 --> 00:11:09,320
had a stress reaction and fainted.

270
00:11:09,320 --> 00:11:10,240
She was sent to the hospital.

271
00:11:10,240 --> 00:11:11,720
She probably won't be able to make it today.

272
00:11:11,720 --> 00:11:12,780
Is it that serious?

273
00:11:12,840 --> 00:11:13,900
Are you kidding me?

274
00:11:13,960 --> 00:11:16,200
I spent the whole morning playing along with you.

275
00:11:16,200 --> 00:11:17,200
A stress reaction?

276
00:11:17,200 --> 00:11:19,080
Isn't that a disease for cats and dogs?

277
00:11:19,080 --> 00:11:19,840
I get it.

278
00:11:19,840 --> 00:11:21,720
You're playing the victim to get more money, right?

279
00:11:21,720 --> 00:11:23,320
Fine, name your price.

280
00:11:23,320 --> 00:11:24,080
No, Mr. Hu.

281
00:11:24,080 --> 00:11:26,080
Maybe I didn't make myself clear.

282
00:11:26,080 --> 00:11:26,960
She fainted.

283
00:11:26,960 --> 00:11:28,600
What does that have to do with me?

284
00:11:28,600 --> 00:11:29,360
Besides,

285
00:11:29,360 --> 00:11:31,200
I had a 40-degree fever at the time.

286
00:11:31,200 --> 00:11:32,240
Because of her,

287
00:11:32,240 --> 00:11:33,720
I didn't have time to take my fever medicine.

288
00:11:33,720 --> 00:11:35,840
The back of my head is still numb.

289
00:11:35,840 --> 00:11:36,720
How do we settle this?

290
00:11:36,720 --> 00:11:37,720
Who cares about me?

291
00:11:37,720 --> 00:11:39,440
Mr. Hu, please calm down.

292
00:11:39,720 --> 00:11:40,960
Didn't we agree on this?

293
00:11:40,960 --> 00:11:42,440
The airline will definitely compensate you.

294
00:11:42,440 --> 00:11:43,320
As for your compensation,

295
00:11:43,320 --> 00:11:44,360
I'll take it if I want it,

296
00:11:44,360 --> 00:11:45,840
and I won't if I don't.

297
00:11:45,840 --> 00:11:47,120
I'm doing you a favor by being here.

298
00:11:47,120 --> 00:11:48,320
Don't push your luck.

299
00:11:48,440 --> 00:11:49,200
No, no.

300
00:11:49,600 --> 00:11:50,120
Mr. Hu,

301
00:11:50,120 --> 00:11:52,200
we are here today to solve the problem,

302
00:11:52,200 --> 00:11:54,320
but the client couldn't come and went to the hospital.

303
00:11:54,320 --> 00:11:56,720
Let's reschedule for a time convenient for you.

304
00:11:56,720 --> 00:11:57,720
It's not convenient for me.

305
00:11:57,720 --> 00:11:58,720
I don't have time to play with you.

306
00:11:58,720 --> 00:11:59,320
I said,

307
00:11:59,320 --> 00:12:01,360
I came here because I don't want to argue with that bitch.

308
00:12:01,360 --> 00:12:02,840
Try insulting my client again.

309
00:12:02,840 --> 00:12:03,600
So what if I insulted her?

310
00:12:03,600 --> 00:12:04,560
I'll insult you too.

311
00:12:04,560 --> 00:12:05,440
Go ahead and insult me.

312
00:12:05,440 --> 00:12:05,970
Go ahead.

313
00:12:06,200 --> 00:12:06,840
Let me see

314
00:12:07,240 --> 00:12:08,320
what you're going to do.

315
00:12:08,320 --> 00:12:08,960
Calm down.

316
00:12:09,120 --> 00:12:10,160
What are you doing?

317
00:12:10,160 --> 00:12:11,080
Law of the People's Republic of China on Public Security Administration Punishments,

318
00:12:11,080 --> 00:12:11,840
Article 43:

319
00:12:11,840 --> 00:12:12,960
Beating another person

320
00:12:12,960 --> 00:12:14,840
or intentionally causing physical injury to another person

321
00:12:14,840 --> 00:12:16,080
shall be punished by administrative detention of not less than five days.

322
00:12:16,080 --> 00:12:18,080
Do you need me to start collecting evidence?

323
00:12:18,080 --> 00:12:18,840
Hu Sheng.

324
00:12:19,200 --> 00:12:21,320
Do you think we're begging for your apology?

325
00:12:21,320 --> 00:12:23,240
We suggested an out-of-court settlement to save time.

326
00:12:23,240 --> 00:12:25,320
You show no sincerity or respect.

327
00:12:25,480 --> 00:12:26,480
Fine. See you in court.

328
00:12:26,480 --> 00:12:27,440
Fine. See you in court.

329
00:12:27,440 --> 00:12:28,370
See you in court.

330
00:12:28,400 --> 00:12:28,840
Lawyer Xiao.

331
00:12:28,840 --> 00:12:29,720
See you in court.

332
00:12:29,720 --> 00:12:30,320
Lawyer Xiao.

333
00:12:30,320 --> 00:12:31,480
I am the victim.

334
00:12:31,480 --> 00:12:32,320
Lawyer Xiao.

335
00:12:32,840 --> 00:12:33,640
What the hell?

336
00:12:33,960 --> 00:12:34,600
Mr. Hu.

337
00:12:37,720 --> 00:12:38,520
He's just like this.

338
00:12:38,520 --> 00:12:39,850
He has this temper. I...

339
00:12:40,320 --> 00:12:41,980
I'll talk some sense into him.

340
00:12:45,720 --> 00:12:46,840
Didn't you say you'd deliver it safely?

341
00:12:46,840 --> 00:12:48,000
Why did you deliver it to the hospital?

342
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:49,320
You promised and swore.

343
00:12:49,320 --> 00:12:50,320
Where did all that go?

344
00:12:50,320 --> 00:12:51,600
They call us an amateur troupe.

345
00:12:51,600 --> 00:12:53,130
And you really act like one.

346
00:12:53,960 --> 00:12:55,480
I... It's my fault.

347
00:12:55,480 --> 00:12:56,200
D-Director.

348
00:12:56,200 --> 00:12:57,600
Director, it's my fault.

349
00:12:57,800 --> 00:12:59,120
I messed up the navigation.

350
00:12:59,120 --> 00:13:00,600
It has nothing to do with them.

351
00:13:00,600 --> 00:13:02,200
I crashed the car. It's my fault.

352
00:13:02,200 --> 00:13:03,200
What's so good about it

353
00:13:03,200 --> 00:13:05,000
that you're all fighting for it?

354
00:13:05,320 --> 00:13:06,800
I'll settle the score with you when I get back.

355
00:13:06,800 --> 00:13:07,560
Where is Jiayi?

356
00:13:07,560 --> 00:13:08,600
She's inside.

357
00:13:08,600 --> 00:13:10,200
Are Xu Jiayi's family members here?

358
00:13:10,200 --> 00:13:12,000
Hello, I'm Jiayi's friend.

359
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:14,200
Hello. You don't need to worry too much.

360
00:13:14,200 --> 00:13:15,930
Your friend had a panic attack.

361
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:17,200
She is resting now,

362
00:13:17,440 --> 00:13:19,240
so just let her recover for a bit.

363
00:13:19,600 --> 00:13:21,320
The patient mentioned she has

364
00:13:21,320 --> 00:13:22,200
ASD (Acute Stress Disorder).

365
00:13:22,200 --> 00:13:22,720
Yes.

366
00:13:23,440 --> 00:13:25,720
Why is it so severe this time?

367
00:13:25,840 --> 00:13:27,080
The psychological burden was too heavy.

368
00:13:27,080 --> 00:13:29,560
Coupled with another external stimulus,

369
00:13:29,560 --> 00:13:32,200
it triggered a strong physical reaction.

370
00:13:32,600 --> 00:13:33,680
Although acute stress disorder

371
00:13:33,680 --> 00:13:34,600
is a

372
00:13:34,600 --> 00:13:37,000
relatively short-term psychological trauma,

373
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:38,440
if not treated promptly

374
00:13:38,440 --> 00:13:40,000
and the stressors are not addressed,

375
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:40,920
it is very likely

376
00:13:40,920 --> 00:13:43,080
to develop into a long-term psychological issue.

377
00:13:43,080 --> 00:13:43,560
Okay.

378
00:13:43,560 --> 00:13:44,360
Thank you.

379
00:13:44,360 --> 00:13:46,080
Alright. Can I go in and see her?

380
00:13:46,080 --> 00:13:46,940
Yes, come on in.

381
00:14:02,320 --> 00:14:04,320
If you were sent by the airline,

382
00:14:04,320 --> 00:14:05,920
save your breath.

383
00:14:06,440 --> 00:14:08,200
Look at the way you were looking at me.

384
00:14:08,200 --> 00:14:09,320
What was that about?

385
00:14:09,320 --> 00:14:11,200
The airline did ask me to talk to you about a settlement.

386
00:14:11,200 --> 00:14:12,320
I knew you wouldn't agree,

387
00:14:12,320 --> 00:14:13,480
so I refused.

388
00:14:14,080 --> 00:14:14,920
Really?

389
00:14:15,920 --> 00:14:17,050
That's more like it.

390
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:18,530
Let's go.

391
00:14:18,560 --> 00:14:19,200
Let's go.

392
00:14:20,720 --> 00:14:22,200
How are you going to fight this?

393
00:14:22,200 --> 00:14:23,320
Two directions.

394
00:14:23,600 --> 00:14:24,720
The first one

395
00:14:25,200 --> 00:14:27,000
is based on tort liability.

396
00:14:27,600 --> 00:14:29,480
But in this direction, it's hard to prove

397
00:14:29,480 --> 00:14:30,360
that Hu Sheng's actions

398
00:14:30,360 --> 00:14:31,720
caused Xu Jiayi's injury

399
00:14:31,720 --> 00:14:32,720
and her illness.

400
00:14:32,960 --> 00:14:34,220
Let's take an example.

401
00:14:34,720 --> 00:14:36,960
A heart disease patient is pushed by someone,

402
00:14:36,960 --> 00:14:38,320
and right at that moment,

403
00:14:38,320 --> 00:14:39,960
he dies of a sudden heart attack.

404
00:14:39,960 --> 00:14:41,240
Can you say

405
00:14:41,480 --> 00:14:43,360
the person who pushed him is a murderer?

406
00:14:43,360 --> 00:14:44,080
No.

407
00:14:44,480 --> 00:14:46,000
Because I can't prove

408
00:14:46,120 --> 00:14:48,200
that the push caused the attack.

409
00:14:48,480 --> 00:14:50,240
So he only needs to bear

410
00:14:50,360 --> 00:14:52,220
the responsibility for the push.

411
00:14:52,480 --> 00:14:53,240
So,

412
00:14:53,360 --> 00:14:56,720
I'm going to fight it as a dispute over the right to life, health,

413
00:14:56,720 --> 00:14:58,720
and bodily integrity.

414
00:14:58,960 --> 00:15:00,960
From this angle, it's not that hard.

415
00:15:01,360 --> 00:15:01,960
As long as you prove

416
00:15:01,960 --> 00:15:03,720
that Xu Jiayi was indeed injured.

417
00:15:03,720 --> 00:15:05,240
But this second method,

418
00:15:05,240 --> 00:15:06,840
compared to the first one,

419
00:15:06,920 --> 00:15:09,480
offers less compensation and protection.

420
00:15:10,320 --> 00:15:11,000
I know.

421
00:15:11,800 --> 00:15:12,860
It doesn't matter.

422
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:15,600
Xu Jiayi just wants his apology anyway.

423
00:15:16,320 --> 00:15:19,200
Also, the judge's subjective inclination is very important.

424
00:15:19,200 --> 00:15:21,080
People have habitual thinking.

425
00:15:21,320 --> 00:15:22,960
Not everyone can understand

426
00:15:23,480 --> 00:15:25,610
that a person's heart can also be hurt.

427
00:15:27,200 --> 00:15:28,200
What's going on?

428
00:15:29,360 --> 00:15:32,200
Why are you so enthusiastic this time?

429
00:15:32,360 --> 00:15:32,960
Am I?

430
00:15:33,360 --> 00:15:34,080
Yes.

431
00:15:34,200 --> 00:15:34,960
Really?

432
00:15:34,960 --> 00:15:35,680
Yes.

433
00:15:35,680 --> 00:15:36,480
What?

434
00:15:37,600 --> 00:15:41,260
You've been in the rain, so you want to hold an umbrella for others?

435
00:15:43,080 --> 00:15:43,840
Alright.

436
00:15:44,120 --> 00:15:44,840
I'm going back.

437
00:15:44,840 --> 00:15:46,440
Call me if you need anything.

438
00:15:50,480 --> 00:15:50,960
Dad,

439
00:15:50,960 --> 00:15:51,690
you're here.

440
00:15:52,920 --> 00:15:54,360
Dinner will be ready soon.

441
00:15:54,360 --> 00:15:55,360
I'll cook a fish.

442
00:16:58,560 --> 00:17:00,720
My client was isolated and helpless in the cabin.

443
00:17:00,720 --> 00:17:02,840
He just wanted to express his dissatisfaction with the service.

444
00:17:02,840 --> 00:17:03,720
How could his act of defending his rights

445
00:17:03,720 --> 00:17:05,079
be escalated by you

446
00:17:05,079 --> 00:17:06,480
to the level of infringement?

447
00:17:06,480 --> 00:17:08,960
There is a world of difference between defending rights and infringement.

448
00:17:08,960 --> 00:17:11,819
Defending rights should be a rational expression,

449
00:17:12,200 --> 00:17:13,720
rather than like the defendant,

450
00:17:13,720 --> 00:17:15,960
threatening others with violence.

451
00:17:16,240 --> 00:17:17,720
Just imagine,

452
00:17:17,839 --> 00:17:19,240
in a confined cabin,

453
00:17:19,560 --> 00:17:22,839
a woman being verbally threatened by a strange man

454
00:17:23,319 --> 00:17:24,920
and repeatedly subjected to

455
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:27,960
his physical touch.

456
00:17:28,359 --> 00:17:31,020
Every second of confrontation in this scenario

457
00:17:31,080 --> 00:17:34,080
is a huge physical and mental strain on my client.

458
00:17:34,320 --> 00:17:35,680
If such behavior

459
00:17:35,800 --> 00:17:38,600
can be sugarcoated as a normal defense of rights,

460
00:17:38,840 --> 00:17:40,170
then I would like to ask,

461
00:17:40,680 --> 00:17:43,000
how can practitioners in the service industry

462
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:44,960
work with peace of mind in the future?

463
00:17:44,960 --> 00:17:46,200
My client's behavior

464
00:17:46,200 --> 00:17:48,320
was just to bring the issue to the plaintiff's attention.

465
00:17:48,320 --> 00:17:50,720
Subjectively, he had no malicious intent to harm the plaintiff.

466
00:17:50,720 --> 00:17:52,600
Shouldn't harm be judged

467
00:17:52,720 --> 00:17:54,960
by the feelings of the victim?

468
00:17:55,440 --> 00:17:57,960
How can it be judged by the perpetrator's intentions?

469
00:17:57,960 --> 00:18:00,840
With just a few words and a few medical certificates,

470
00:18:00,840 --> 00:18:01,600
who can guarantee

471
00:18:01,600 --> 00:18:03,960
that the plaintiff is not exaggerating to win the case?

472
00:18:03,960 --> 00:18:06,600
Mental damage is not a subjective judgment.

473
00:18:06,600 --> 00:18:07,320
The Civil Code of the People's Republic of China

474
00:18:07,320 --> 00:18:08,720
explicitly includes it

475
00:18:08,720 --> 00:18:10,600
in the scope of personal rights protection.

476
00:18:10,600 --> 00:18:11,600
This is the law's rigid protection

477
00:18:11,600 --> 00:18:13,960
of human dignity.

478
00:18:14,480 --> 00:18:16,440
Neither party agrees to mediation.

479
00:18:16,440 --> 00:18:19,640
The verdict of this case will be announced at a later date.

480
00:18:33,120 --> 00:18:34,480
Is the verdict out?

481
00:18:34,880 --> 00:18:36,040
Let's see. Hurry.

482
00:18:37,680 --> 00:18:41,160
The defendant, Hu Sheng, during the plane's landing,

483
00:18:41,160 --> 00:18:43,240
had a conflict with the plaintiff, Xu Jiayi,

484
00:18:43,240 --> 00:18:45,480
and proceeded to tear the plaintiff's name tag,

485
00:18:45,480 --> 00:18:47,010
causing her clothes to rip.

486
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:50,640
He shall apologize to the plaintiff according to the law.

487
00:18:50,640 --> 00:18:51,800
A public apology is a must.

488
00:18:51,800 --> 00:18:53,240
See? That's why Lawyer Xiao is awesome.

489
00:18:53,240 --> 00:18:53,560
Yeah.

490
00:18:53,560 --> 00:18:55,560
He wins every case he takes.

491
00:18:55,560 --> 00:18:56,200
Right?

492
00:18:58,560 --> 00:19:01,160
Why the long face? Still holding a grudge?

493
00:19:01,360 --> 00:19:02,480
Let me do a dance to calm you down.

494
00:19:02,480 --> 00:19:03,800
I just learned it today.

495
00:19:03,800 --> 00:19:06,720
Uncle, there's still a paragraph left unread.

496
00:19:06,960 --> 00:19:08,040
There's more?

497
00:19:08,200 --> 00:19:11,040
Because the plaintiff, Xu Jiayi, failed to provide evidence...

498
00:19:11,040 --> 00:19:14,640
Proving that she suffered mental distress due to this incident.

499
00:19:16,120 --> 00:19:17,040
The claims for lost wages and mental distress compensation under Paragraph 1 of Article 165,

500
00:19:17,040 --> 00:19:18,680
Articles 1110, 1003, 1004, and Paragraph 1 of Article 1117

501
00:19:18,680 --> 00:19:20,560
are denied.

502
00:19:20,720 --> 00:19:21,560
This means

503
00:19:21,800 --> 00:19:23,480
the court didn't acknowledge

504
00:19:23,480 --> 00:19:25,740
that Xu Jiayi suffered mental distress,

505
00:19:26,040 --> 00:19:28,880
nor do they believe her psychological trauma

506
00:19:28,880 --> 00:19:32,140
has a direct causal relationship with Hu Sheng's actions.

507
00:19:32,360 --> 00:19:34,160
If they don't acknowledge it, so be it.

508
00:19:34,160 --> 00:19:35,920
Let's not be too serious about it.

509
00:19:35,920 --> 00:19:37,280
Anyway, Xu Jiayi wanted an apology,

510
00:19:37,280 --> 00:19:38,280
and the court ordered it.

511
00:19:38,280 --> 00:19:39,240
So that's it.

512
00:19:39,240 --> 00:19:40,400
What do you mean that's it?

513
00:19:40,400 --> 00:19:41,560
What's wrong with being serious?

514
00:19:41,560 --> 00:19:43,280
The law is supposed to be serious.

515
00:19:43,280 --> 00:19:43,800
Besides,

516
00:19:43,800 --> 00:19:44,640
such a verdict

517
00:19:44,720 --> 00:19:47,040
is a secondary injury to Xu Jiayi.

518
00:19:47,280 --> 00:19:48,560
And that guy Hu Sheng,

519
00:19:48,560 --> 00:19:50,280
do you think he'll apologize sincerely?

520
00:19:50,280 --> 00:19:51,120
Can you?

521
00:19:56,680 --> 00:19:57,940
What's wrong, sister?

522
00:20:01,280 --> 00:20:04,340
Hu Sheng's lawyer said he is willing to pay 10,000 yuan.

523
00:20:04,680 --> 00:20:06,280
But he refuses to apologize.

524
00:20:06,280 --> 00:20:08,400
Does he think I only want money?

525
00:20:08,480 --> 00:20:10,410
I'm not doing this for money at all.

526
00:20:10,440 --> 00:20:11,800
It's okay, Jiayi.

527
00:20:12,040 --> 00:20:13,560
If you are not satisfied with this result,

528
00:20:13,560 --> 00:20:14,960
we will continue to appeal.

529
00:20:14,960 --> 00:20:15,800
Appeal?

530
00:20:16,040 --> 00:20:17,560
We will present new evidence,

531
00:20:17,560 --> 00:20:19,890
submit more detailed and clear evidence,

532
00:20:19,960 --> 00:20:21,760
and ask the court to reconsider.

533
00:20:21,800 --> 00:20:22,680
Of course.

534
00:20:22,960 --> 00:20:23,800
Then this case

535
00:20:23,800 --> 00:20:25,560
might drag on longer.

536
00:20:26,280 --> 00:20:28,560
You might also face more difficulties.

537
00:20:28,680 --> 00:20:30,800
So you need to think it through.

538
00:20:35,920 --> 00:20:38,450
I don't want to let it go unresolved like this.

539
00:20:40,720 --> 00:20:41,560
Lawyer Xiao,

540
00:20:43,200 --> 00:20:44,400
I trust you.

541
00:20:44,960 --> 00:20:45,960
I want to appeal.

542
00:20:47,880 --> 00:20:48,960
It's a scam.

543
00:20:49,760 --> 00:20:51,680
Two bitches are running a scam.

544
00:20:51,680 --> 00:20:52,800
They think it's not enough money.

545
00:20:52,800 --> 00:20:53,520
What do you call this?

546
00:20:53,520 --> 00:20:54,920
This is pushing their luck.

547
00:20:54,920 --> 00:20:56,720
This is being ungrateful.

548
00:20:59,040 --> 00:21:00,040
Calm down. I...

549
00:21:00,040 --> 00:21:00,970
Wanna play, huh?

550
00:21:01,280 --> 00:21:03,680
Fine. I'll play along to the end.

551
00:21:04,280 --> 00:21:06,200
Here's the plan. You write something.

552
00:21:06,200 --> 00:21:07,480
I'll post it online too.

553
00:21:07,480 --> 00:21:08,280
I refuse to believe

554
00:21:08,280 --> 00:21:09,960
I can't beat two little girls.

555
00:21:12,560 --> 00:21:14,960
One, two, three. Action.

556
00:21:18,200 --> 00:21:19,520
My name is Hu Sheng.

557
00:21:20,760 --> 00:21:24,560
I'm the person involved in the recent flight dispute.

558
00:21:25,520 --> 00:21:27,440
If I weren't forced to,

559
00:21:27,560 --> 00:21:30,760
I wouldn't have recorded this video and posted it online.

560
00:21:31,960 --> 00:21:32,760
See?

561
00:21:33,480 --> 00:21:34,720
The court ruled

562
00:21:35,280 --> 00:21:37,960
that this flight attendant's mental distress

563
00:21:38,200 --> 00:21:40,200
has nothing to do with me.

564
00:21:40,480 --> 00:21:41,960
But I never expected

565
00:21:42,160 --> 00:21:43,480
that she wouldn't let it go.

566
00:21:43,480 --> 00:21:45,200
She colluded with her lawyer

567
00:21:45,280 --> 00:21:46,960
and actually appealed against me.

568
00:21:46,960 --> 00:21:48,960
As a law-abiding citizen,

569
00:21:49,200 --> 00:21:51,440
I decided to sue this flight attendant

570
00:21:51,480 --> 00:21:54,200
and Star Alliance Airlines at the same time.

571
00:21:54,240 --> 00:21:55,240
This scumbag

572
00:21:55,240 --> 00:21:57,170
is treating himself as the victim.

573
00:21:57,480 --> 00:21:59,720
The comments are completely one-sided now.

574
00:21:59,720 --> 00:22:01,960
Netizens don't even distinguish right from wrong.

575
00:22:01,960 --> 00:22:03,960
This is purely the guilty party complaining first.

576
00:22:03,960 --> 00:22:05,680
If he feels wronged,

577
00:22:05,720 --> 00:22:07,280
it's actually not surprising.

578
00:22:07,280 --> 00:22:08,160
People

579
00:22:08,240 --> 00:22:10,800
always like to think from their own perspective.

580
00:22:10,800 --> 00:22:12,400
But no matter what he thinks,

581
00:22:12,800 --> 00:22:13,960
during the second trial,

582
00:22:13,960 --> 00:22:16,200
we must prove the harm he caused.

583
00:22:16,880 --> 00:22:18,480
And make him apologize publicly.

584
00:22:18,480 --> 00:22:20,400
Yes, he must apologize publicly.

585
00:22:20,760 --> 00:22:21,400
Right.

586
00:22:21,880 --> 00:22:23,080
This video by Hu Sheng

587
00:22:23,680 --> 00:22:25,640
has already had an extremely negative impact

588
00:22:25,640 --> 00:22:27,240
on the company's image.

589
00:22:28,200 --> 00:22:30,130
Our investment in brand promotion

590
00:22:30,440 --> 00:22:31,800
has all gone down the drain.

591
00:22:31,800 --> 00:22:33,200
We can't even handle

592
00:22:33,200 --> 00:22:34,680
the recent customer complaints.

593
00:22:34,680 --> 00:22:37,280
This kind of situation has never happened before.

594
00:22:37,280 --> 00:22:40,120
Why hasn't such a small matter been resolved yet?

595
00:22:40,200 --> 00:22:41,600
It's even getting worse.

596
00:22:41,880 --> 00:22:43,160
We invited Lawyer Li here today

597
00:22:43,160 --> 00:22:44,440
to solve this matter.

598
00:22:44,960 --> 00:22:45,960
Please rest assured, everyone.

599
00:22:45,960 --> 00:22:47,680
We will contact Hu Sheng as soon as possible

600
00:22:47,680 --> 00:22:49,120
and ask him to take down this video.

601
00:22:49,120 --> 00:22:51,050
Isn't it just a public opinion war?

602
00:22:51,200 --> 00:22:52,680
Let's fight him to the end.

603
00:22:52,720 --> 00:22:55,280
Issue an announcement, send a lawyer's letter,

604
00:22:55,280 --> 00:22:56,800
and sue him for defamation.

605
00:22:56,800 --> 00:22:58,960
Then find a few marketing accounts to hype it up.

606
00:22:58,960 --> 00:23:00,560
Public opinion is a variable,

607
00:23:00,560 --> 00:23:02,400
but the law is a constant.

608
00:23:02,480 --> 00:23:05,680
If we rely on inciting public opinion to influence the case,

609
00:23:05,680 --> 00:23:08,000
it will not only interfere with judicial justice

610
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:09,240
but also backfire.

611
00:23:09,480 --> 00:23:10,240
Right.

612
00:23:10,440 --> 00:23:13,240
And I hope everyone understands one thing.

613
00:23:14,240 --> 00:23:15,960
What Xu Jiayi is suffering from now

614
00:23:15,960 --> 00:23:17,360
is psychological trauma.

615
00:23:17,360 --> 00:23:20,440
Public pressure is more likely to worsen it,

616
00:23:20,680 --> 00:23:21,480
perhaps becoming

617
00:23:21,480 --> 00:23:23,280
the last straw that crushes her,

618
00:23:23,360 --> 00:23:25,760
pushing things further out of control.

619
00:23:25,760 --> 00:23:27,960
There's no need to appeal.

620
00:23:28,720 --> 00:23:29,800
It's not a big deal.

621
00:23:29,960 --> 00:23:31,480
Why is she blowing it out of proportion

622
00:23:31,480 --> 00:23:32,680
and making such a fuss?

623
00:23:32,680 --> 00:23:35,200
This kid has indeed been wronged.

624
00:23:35,200 --> 00:23:37,040
I'll talk to her again.

625
00:23:37,680 --> 00:23:40,400
The important thing is to smooth things over.

626
00:23:40,720 --> 00:23:43,040
Understood. I'll handle it properly.

627
00:23:43,640 --> 00:23:44,720
None of these executives

628
00:23:44,720 --> 00:23:46,200
are truly considering Xu Jiayi's perspective.

629
00:23:46,200 --> 00:23:47,480
Thinking about the problem.

630
00:23:47,480 --> 00:23:48,480
That's for sure.

631
00:23:48,680 --> 00:23:49,480
For them,

632
00:23:49,480 --> 00:23:51,960
the most important thing is that their own interests are not damaged.

633
00:23:51,960 --> 00:23:53,680
They don't care about anyone else.

634
00:23:53,680 --> 00:23:55,720
You know, Hu Sheng is really interesting,

635
00:23:55,720 --> 00:23:57,200
even playing the public opinion card.

636
00:23:57,200 --> 00:23:59,440
Making endless fuss over such a small matter.

637
00:23:59,440 --> 00:24:00,160
Lawyer Su.

638
00:24:00,680 --> 00:24:02,680
I don't think this is a small matter.

639
00:24:03,000 --> 00:24:03,800
I didn't mean that.

640
00:24:03,800 --> 00:24:06,200
I definitely stand with Xu Jiayi on this.

641
00:24:06,200 --> 00:24:06,960
Bowen.

642
00:24:10,440 --> 00:24:11,200
Please prepare

643
00:24:11,200 --> 00:24:13,120
the detailed materials of Husheng Company for me.

644
00:24:13,120 --> 00:24:13,850
Understood.

645
00:24:17,240 --> 00:24:18,240
Jiayi,

646
00:24:18,440 --> 00:24:20,520
why don't you drop that lawsuit?

647
00:24:20,560 --> 00:24:21,760
Listen to Mom.

648
00:24:22,000 --> 00:24:24,360
It's not worth all this trouble

649
00:24:24,440 --> 00:24:25,720
over such a small matter.

650
00:24:25,720 --> 00:24:26,720
What if it blows up

651
00:24:26,840 --> 00:24:28,720
and affects your work?

652
00:24:28,800 --> 00:24:31,040
Is it really necessary to fight to the end over this?

653
00:24:31,040 --> 00:24:32,000
She's just asking for trouble.

654
00:24:32,000 --> 00:24:33,000
So stupid.

655
00:24:33,000 --> 00:24:34,280
I would have moved on long ago.

656
00:24:34,280 --> 00:24:35,200
I guess she's just a scammer.

657
00:24:35,200 --> 00:24:36,320
Didn't the court already make a ruling?

658
00:24:36,320 --> 00:24:36,920
Why is this still going on?

659
00:24:36,920 --> 00:24:38,920
It's a perfect match for Xingmeng to have such a flight attendant.

660
00:24:38,920 --> 00:24:40,400
This airline is usually so arrogant.

661
00:24:40,400 --> 00:24:41,600
Such a small matter, yet it's trending every day.

662
00:24:41,600 --> 00:24:43,240
What kind of entitled princess is this?

663
00:24:43,240 --> 00:24:44,160
It must be a publicity stunt.

664
00:24:44,160 --> 00:24:45,040
She's desperate for fame.

665
00:24:45,040 --> 00:24:46,720
She didn't expect to mess with the wrong person, did she?

666
00:24:46,720 --> 00:24:47,480
Is it really necessary

667
00:24:47,480 --> 00:24:49,080
to drag this out for so long?

668
00:25:30,680 --> 00:25:32,340
Are you feeling better today?

669
00:25:35,120 --> 00:25:36,380
About your situation,

670
00:25:36,840 --> 00:25:38,080
I've already spoken to the management.

671
00:25:38,080 --> 00:25:39,720
It wasn't your fault to begin with.

672
00:25:39,720 --> 00:25:41,120
In the service industry,

673
00:25:41,360 --> 00:25:44,420
our biggest fear is running into scoundrels like that.

674
00:25:44,600 --> 00:25:45,560
Thank you.

675
00:25:47,320 --> 00:25:48,280
You know what?

676
00:25:48,840 --> 00:25:51,320
I've actually always really liked you.

677
00:25:51,320 --> 00:25:52,800
You're young,

678
00:25:53,120 --> 00:25:54,160
but at work,

679
00:25:54,520 --> 00:25:55,960
you're hardworking, serious,

680
00:25:55,960 --> 00:25:58,220
responsible, patient, and persistent.

681
00:25:58,760 --> 00:26:00,560
I've told the management several times

682
00:26:00,560 --> 00:26:01,760
to promote you.

683
00:26:03,400 --> 00:26:04,240
Jiayi,

684
00:26:05,080 --> 00:26:06,880
getting to where we are now

685
00:26:07,280 --> 00:26:08,280
wasn't easy.

686
00:26:08,440 --> 00:26:11,900
There's no need to ruin your future over such trivial matters.

687
00:26:14,360 --> 00:26:15,160
Manager.

688
00:26:16,160 --> 00:26:18,890
Are you trying to persuade me to drop the lawsuit?

689
00:26:20,240 --> 00:26:21,040
This time,

690
00:26:22,160 --> 00:26:23,560
you were indeed wronged.

691
00:26:24,480 --> 00:26:26,810
But if this matter continues to escalate,

692
00:26:27,240 --> 00:26:29,200
the damage to the company's brand

693
00:26:29,200 --> 00:26:30,480
will be immeasurable.

694
00:26:32,720 --> 00:26:34,520
Let me tell you from the bottom of my heart.

695
00:26:34,520 --> 00:26:36,280
I also started as a flight attendant

696
00:26:36,280 --> 00:26:38,120
and worked my way up to this position.

697
00:26:38,120 --> 00:26:40,200
There's an old saying in our industry:

698
00:26:40,200 --> 00:26:43,560
Which flight attendant hasn't cried on a plane a few times?

699
00:26:47,200 --> 00:26:48,200
Wipe your tears.

700
00:26:49,280 --> 00:26:50,520
Let it go.

701
00:27:43,560 --> 00:27:44,440
Thank you.

702
00:27:53,440 --> 00:27:55,120
When I'm in a bad mood,

703
00:27:55,160 --> 00:27:57,440
I like to come here for a walk and relax.

704
00:28:03,320 --> 00:28:04,080
Have a seat.

705
00:28:08,720 --> 00:28:09,840
Ms. Xiao.

706
00:28:10,440 --> 00:28:12,880
People online are cursing me right now.

707
00:28:13,440 --> 00:28:16,240
The company also thinks I'm causing them trouble.

708
00:28:16,400 --> 00:28:18,200
Even my closest family members,

709
00:28:18,720 --> 00:28:20,180
they don't understand me.

710
00:28:22,320 --> 00:28:23,360
I don't know

711
00:28:23,840 --> 00:28:26,240
if I'm really too fragile, too dramatic,

712
00:28:26,240 --> 00:28:27,760
or just making a fuss over nothing.

713
00:28:27,760 --> 00:28:29,200
Of course you're not.

714
00:28:30,560 --> 00:28:31,760
You have to firmly believe

715
00:28:31,760 --> 00:28:34,480
that all your feelings are real.

716
00:28:35,320 --> 00:28:39,040
Just like this grass, these trees,

717
00:28:41,000 --> 00:28:42,120
and this breeze.

718
00:28:45,400 --> 00:28:46,200
Jiayi.

719
00:28:49,320 --> 00:28:51,200
You're actually really brave,

720
00:28:51,920 --> 00:28:53,520
braver than I expected.

721
00:28:54,200 --> 00:28:57,200
You dare to face your true emotions,

722
00:28:58,640 --> 00:29:00,560
and dare to fight for those little things

723
00:29:00,560 --> 00:29:03,320
that others say aren't worth mentioning.

724
00:29:07,120 --> 00:29:08,320
Thank you, Ms. Xiao.

725
00:29:09,880 --> 00:29:12,560
If it were you,

726
00:29:13,280 --> 00:29:14,540
what would you choose?

727
00:29:14,960 --> 00:29:15,760
Me?

728
00:29:18,520 --> 00:29:20,120
What would I choose?

729
00:29:22,240 --> 00:29:23,880
I always remember a saying.

730
00:29:24,120 --> 00:29:25,560
It roughly means,

731
00:29:25,800 --> 00:29:29,040
in the face of things that make you cry,

732
00:29:29,560 --> 00:29:31,960
you could have chosen to shout it out.

733
00:29:33,440 --> 00:29:36,280
Yes, then you should shout it out.

734
00:29:37,600 --> 00:29:39,560
As long as you bravely shout it out,

735
00:29:40,200 --> 00:29:41,000
I believe

736
00:29:41,960 --> 00:29:45,920
the world will definitely hear a little bit of that voice.

737
00:29:47,160 --> 00:29:48,440
And then maybe,

738
00:29:49,200 --> 00:29:51,130
someone will shout along with you.

739
00:29:54,000 --> 00:29:56,260
As long as there are more people shouting

740
00:29:56,480 --> 00:29:57,880
and fewer people crying,

741
00:29:58,840 --> 00:30:02,760
then those things that were originally impossible to change

742
00:30:03,680 --> 00:30:05,200
might just be changed.

743
00:30:07,960 --> 00:30:09,000
This case

744
00:30:09,760 --> 00:30:11,760
is facing quite a lot of resistance.

745
00:30:12,760 --> 00:30:13,560
So,

746
00:30:14,120 --> 00:30:16,850
I respect whatever choice and decision you make.

747
00:30:16,880 --> 00:30:18,040
Just do one thing.

748
00:30:19,120 --> 00:30:21,160
Listen to the voice in your heart.

749
00:30:21,840 --> 00:30:23,840
No matter what decision you make,

750
00:30:25,240 --> 00:30:27,160
I will firmly stand with you.

751
00:30:29,440 --> 00:30:30,720
Thank you, Ms. Xiao.

752
00:30:35,840 --> 00:30:37,040
I don't want to give up.

753
00:30:37,040 --> 00:30:38,320
Then let's not give up.

754
00:30:51,320 --> 00:30:53,320
The flight attendant hasn't dropped the lawsuit yet.

755
00:30:53,320 --> 00:30:54,120
Not yet.

756
00:30:55,800 --> 00:30:57,600
Then hire more internet trolls.

757
00:30:57,680 --> 00:30:58,360
I don't believe

758
00:30:58,360 --> 00:31:00,090
we can't beat two little girls.

759
00:31:00,840 --> 00:31:01,680
Come in.

760
00:31:01,760 --> 00:31:03,400
Mr. Hu, Lawyer Li Xin is here.

761
00:31:03,400 --> 00:31:04,760
He says he wants to talk to you.

762
00:31:04,760 --> 00:31:05,840
Tell him I'm not here.

763
00:31:05,840 --> 00:31:07,800
Mr. Hu, are you busy?

764
00:31:08,600 --> 00:31:09,360
Lawyer Li.

765
00:31:09,840 --> 00:31:10,840
Come in, come in.

766
00:31:10,840 --> 00:31:12,520
Mr. Hu and I are having a meeting.

767
00:31:12,520 --> 00:31:13,480
Please have a seat.

768
00:31:13,480 --> 00:31:14,480
I'm sorry, Mr. Hu.

769
00:31:14,480 --> 00:31:15,610
Sorry to bother you.

770
00:31:17,640 --> 00:31:20,280
If you're here on behalf of Star Alliance Airlines,

771
00:31:20,280 --> 00:31:21,400
I don't think we need to talk.

772
00:31:21,400 --> 00:31:22,200
You can leave.

773
00:31:22,800 --> 00:31:24,330
I won't take down the video.

774
00:31:24,680 --> 00:31:25,840
I want to defend my rights,

775
00:31:25,840 --> 00:31:26,840
and I will defend them to the end.

776
00:31:26,840 --> 00:31:29,600
Mr. Hu, I advise you not to be so certain.

777
00:31:30,680 --> 00:31:31,340
Who are you?

778
00:31:32,120 --> 00:31:33,780
What kind of attitude is that?

779
00:31:35,040 --> 00:31:36,520
I'm just looking out for you.

780
00:31:36,520 --> 00:31:38,240
I'm afraid you'll regret it later.

781
00:31:38,240 --> 00:31:39,560
What could I possibly regret?

782
00:31:39,560 --> 00:31:41,000
What... is this it?

783
00:31:41,080 --> 00:31:44,040
The cooperation we agreed on with Wangang has been suspended.

784
00:31:44,040 --> 00:31:45,170
Are they kidding me?

785
00:31:45,440 --> 00:31:47,720
They said it was their legal counsel's advice.

786
00:31:47,720 --> 00:31:50,160
They need to reassess the cooperation risks.

787
00:31:50,160 --> 00:31:52,420
Which bastard is the lawyer for Wangang?

788
00:31:52,720 --> 00:31:53,320
Mr. Hu.

789
00:31:55,560 --> 00:31:57,080
I am that bastard.

790
00:31:59,080 --> 00:31:59,720
Well...

791
00:31:59,720 --> 00:32:00,640
I've heard for a long time

792
00:32:00,640 --> 00:32:02,280
that Honghu is Wangang's legal counsel.

793
00:32:02,280 --> 00:32:03,280
So Lawyer Li is

794
00:32:03,280 --> 00:32:05,280
Wangang's chief legal counsel.

795
00:32:05,280 --> 00:32:07,240
I'm not here representing Xingmeng today.

796
00:32:07,240 --> 00:32:09,040
I'm here representing Wangang.

797
00:32:10,000 --> 00:32:11,360
Well, what would you two like to drink?

798
00:32:11,360 --> 00:32:12,280
I'll have someone bring it over right away.

799
00:32:12,280 --> 00:32:13,280
No need to bother.

800
00:32:13,400 --> 00:32:15,930
Lawyer Li has other things to attend to later.

801
00:32:16,600 --> 00:32:17,600
Okay, no problem.

802
00:32:18,320 --> 00:32:20,960
You're throwing your weight around here using someone else's name.

803
00:32:20,960 --> 00:32:24,400
I've been helping Wangang conduct due diligence on their partners recently,

804
00:32:24,400 --> 00:32:25,840
to eliminate legal risks,

805
00:32:25,840 --> 00:32:27,640
including reputational risks.

806
00:32:28,280 --> 00:32:30,840
It just so happens that your company, Mr. Hu, is within the scope of our due diligence,

807
00:32:30,840 --> 00:32:33,600
but the reputational risk ranks first.

808
00:32:34,880 --> 00:32:36,210
Are you threatening me?

809
00:32:36,760 --> 00:32:37,920
You're overstating it.

810
00:32:37,920 --> 00:32:40,650
Wangang Group has always valued its reputation.

811
00:32:41,120 --> 00:32:43,440
But your recent videos online

812
00:32:43,920 --> 00:32:45,440
have generated a lot of buzz.

813
00:32:45,440 --> 00:32:46,960
If you continue to hype them up,

814
00:32:46,960 --> 00:32:49,400
I'm afraid it will affect your cooperation with Wangang.

815
00:32:49,400 --> 00:32:51,200
I'm doing this for your own good.

816
00:33:02,160 --> 00:33:03,290
Please consider it.

817
00:33:11,640 --> 00:33:12,880
Lawyer Li, Lawyer Li, Lawyer Li.

818
00:33:12,880 --> 00:33:14,600
We're leaving, we're leaving.

819
00:33:14,600 --> 00:33:17,530
Mr. Hu was just driven crazy by the flight attendant.

820
00:33:17,880 --> 00:33:19,280
What time are we leaving?

821
00:33:22,720 --> 00:33:23,280
Six o'clock.

822
00:33:23,280 --> 00:33:23,800
Five o'clock.

823
00:33:23,800 --> 00:33:24,040
Five.

824
00:33:24,040 --> 00:33:26,240
Thank you for your cooperation, Mr. Hu.

825
00:33:26,400 --> 00:33:27,560
Forty-four minutes left.

826
00:33:27,560 --> 00:33:28,120
Okay.

827
00:33:29,040 --> 00:33:29,840
Forty-three.

828
00:33:31,800 --> 00:33:32,440
This...

829
00:33:47,760 --> 00:33:48,820
What are you doing?

830
00:33:48,840 --> 00:33:51,400
No, seeing Hu Sheng looking so frustrated,

831
00:33:51,440 --> 00:33:52,600
I really enjoyed it.

832
00:33:53,680 --> 00:33:56,040
Lawyer Li, that was a new trick today.

833
00:33:56,880 --> 00:33:58,920
Using their own force against them, right?

834
00:33:58,920 --> 00:33:59,960
I learned something.

835
00:33:59,960 --> 00:34:02,000
Your riding on my coattails wasn't bad either.

836
00:34:02,000 --> 00:34:03,200
There are still over forty minutes left.

837
00:34:03,200 --> 00:34:04,000
Forty-three.

838
00:34:04,640 --> 00:34:05,970
That really hit a nerve.

839
00:34:06,680 --> 00:34:08,080
I learned it all from you.

840
00:34:09,920 --> 00:34:11,120
No, what I meant was,

841
00:34:11,120 --> 00:34:12,120
didn't we also

842
00:34:12,120 --> 00:34:13,780
indirectly help Xiao Longnv?

843
00:34:14,000 --> 00:34:15,639
I really hope she wins this time.

844
00:34:15,639 --> 00:34:17,040
Xu Jiayi is so pitiful.

845
00:34:17,679 --> 00:34:18,480
Why don't you use this sympathy

846
00:34:18,480 --> 00:34:20,280
on Aunt Fang?

847
00:34:26,600 --> 00:34:27,199
Director.

848
00:34:27,800 --> 00:34:29,320
These are the successful precedents of similar cases

849
00:34:29,320 --> 00:34:31,280
I've collected over the past three years.

850
00:34:31,280 --> 00:34:32,080
Take a look.

851
00:34:32,880 --> 00:34:34,000
Sister, I've looked at them too.

852
00:34:34,000 --> 00:34:35,800
I think we have a great chance.

853
00:34:36,520 --> 00:34:37,600
I think

854
00:34:37,719 --> 00:34:38,840
we shouldn't just look at the successful ones,

855
00:34:38,840 --> 00:34:40,480
we should also look at the failed ones

856
00:34:40,480 --> 00:34:42,280
to manage our own expectations.

857
00:34:42,280 --> 00:34:43,960
What expectations?

858
00:34:43,960 --> 00:34:46,280
Jiayi is very determined about this.

859
00:34:46,280 --> 00:34:47,960
Can you stop being so pessimistic?

860
00:34:47,960 --> 00:34:48,960
Yeah, Uncle.

861
00:34:49,000 --> 00:34:50,639
Why are you pouring cold water on us?

862
00:34:50,639 --> 00:34:52,560
I'm just telling the truth.

863
00:34:52,560 --> 00:34:54,000
This case is hard to fight.

864
00:34:54,000 --> 00:34:54,880
Once it starts,

865
00:34:54,960 --> 00:34:56,120
if Hu Sheng records another video

866
00:34:56,120 --> 00:34:57,440
and talks nonsense on the internet,

867
00:34:57,440 --> 00:34:59,600
if he causes any more trouble,

868
00:34:59,640 --> 00:35:01,840
it will be even more hurtful to Xu Jiayi.

869
00:35:02,080 --> 00:35:02,800
Alright.

870
00:35:03,240 --> 00:35:04,240
Stop arguing.

871
00:35:04,760 --> 00:35:06,360
Regarding the second trial,

872
00:35:06,400 --> 00:35:07,840
let me arrange our strategy.

873
00:35:07,840 --> 00:35:09,320
There are two main tasks.

874
00:35:09,320 --> 00:35:12,400
First, we need to make the judge believe

875
00:35:12,400 --> 00:35:15,000
that this psychological trauma is real.

876
00:35:15,280 --> 00:35:16,480
Second,

877
00:35:16,600 --> 00:35:18,330
we need to make the judge accept

878
00:35:18,480 --> 00:35:21,920
that Jiayi's psychological trauma was caused by Hu Sheng.

879
00:35:23,080 --> 00:35:24,040
How do we make the judge accept it?

880
00:35:24,040 --> 00:35:25,400
Do I force the judge?

881
00:35:25,600 --> 00:35:27,330
What does it have to do with you?

882
00:35:27,600 --> 00:35:29,360
We need to hire a psychological expert

883
00:35:29,360 --> 00:35:32,400
to persuade the judge from a professional perspective.

884
00:35:32,400 --> 00:35:33,760
Okay, Director, I'll check right away.

885
00:35:33,760 --> 00:35:34,760
I'll go check too.

886
00:35:35,520 --> 00:35:36,760
Such an elite team.

887
00:35:41,240 --> 00:35:42,000
Sister Long.

888
00:35:42,160 --> 00:35:43,800
Hu Sheng deleted that video.

889
00:35:45,240 --> 00:35:46,160
Did he find his conscience?

890
00:35:46,160 --> 00:35:48,640
Come on, what conscience could he have?

891
00:35:50,240 --> 00:35:51,160
I know.

892
00:35:51,320 --> 00:35:53,920
It must be Lawyer Li representing the airline

893
00:35:53,920 --> 00:35:54,850
who stopped him.

894
00:35:55,480 --> 00:35:57,000
Good job, Lawyer Li.

895
00:36:13,680 --> 00:36:14,940
Wait a minute, you two.

896
00:36:15,040 --> 00:36:16,920
Why do you say he was the one who stopped it?

897
00:36:16,920 --> 00:36:19,560
Because Lawyer Li is better than you.

898
00:36:20,360 --> 00:36:21,760
And he's taller than you.

899
00:36:22,680 --> 00:36:25,520
Fine, my two colleagues. Rent goes up next month.

900
00:36:25,880 --> 00:36:27,680
Look at him, Sister Long.

901
00:36:30,600 --> 00:36:32,730
Lawyer Li, the video has been deleted.

902
00:36:34,160 --> 00:36:34,920
Got it.

903
00:36:35,480 --> 00:36:36,560
Let him show off.

904
00:36:38,160 --> 00:36:38,760
Lawyer Li.

905
00:36:39,920 --> 00:36:42,720
I don't think I've seen this smile of yours before.

906
00:36:43,160 --> 00:36:44,400
It's so sunny.

907
00:36:45,640 --> 00:36:46,120
Wasn't I

908
00:36:46,120 --> 00:36:46,960
sunny before?

909
00:36:58,560 --> 00:37:01,560
Many people don't understand acute stress reaction.

910
00:37:01,880 --> 00:37:04,740
It's actually the body's survival instinct switch

911
00:37:04,880 --> 00:37:06,480
when facing a sudden crisis.

912
00:37:06,960 --> 00:37:09,090
It can manifest as somatic reactions,

913
00:37:09,440 --> 00:37:10,560
nausea, vomiting,

914
00:37:10,680 --> 00:37:12,040
numbness in hands and feet,

915
00:37:12,040 --> 00:37:14,440
and alkalosis caused by hyperventilation.

916
00:37:14,440 --> 00:37:16,960
Some people even have dissociative symptoms.

917
00:37:16,960 --> 00:37:18,120
Sometimes, wounds of the mind

918
00:37:18,120 --> 00:37:19,050
I'm telling you,

919
00:37:19,320 --> 00:37:20,320
Director Zhuge

920
00:37:20,320 --> 00:37:23,080
is indeed the most authoritative psychological expert in the province.

921
00:37:23,080 --> 00:37:24,120
He speaks really well.

922
00:37:24,120 --> 00:37:27,040
can trigger overactivation of the brain's amygdala.

923
00:37:27,040 --> 00:37:28,560
Damaging nerve cells

924
00:37:28,720 --> 00:37:30,440
and causing chronic trauma.

925
00:37:34,360 --> 00:37:35,240
Dean Zhuge,

926
00:37:35,680 --> 00:37:37,280
I'm here to bother you again.

927
00:37:37,440 --> 00:37:38,560
That was a wonderful lecture.

928
00:37:38,560 --> 00:37:40,760
Class ended before I could hear enough.

929
00:37:41,360 --> 00:37:43,440
This is the person I mentioned on the phone,

930
00:37:43,440 --> 00:37:45,320
my old classmate, Lawyer Xiao Longnv.

931
00:37:45,320 --> 00:37:46,320
Hello, Dean.

932
00:37:46,320 --> 00:37:47,450
Hello, Xiao Longnv.

933
00:37:47,720 --> 00:37:48,560
Mr. Tian,

934
00:37:48,600 --> 00:37:50,000
I told you on the phone.

935
00:37:50,000 --> 00:37:52,240
I'm not interested in testifying in court.

936
00:37:52,240 --> 00:37:54,440
Do you want to hear about our case

937
00:37:54,440 --> 00:37:55,680
before you make a decision?

938
00:37:55,680 --> 00:37:57,920
I won't testify no matter what the case is.

939
00:37:57,920 --> 00:38:00,000
I just want to focus on my academic research.

940
00:38:00,000 --> 00:38:01,560
Don't worry. This case

941
00:38:01,560 --> 00:38:03,640
won't take up too much of your time and energy.

942
00:38:03,640 --> 00:38:04,960
Please reconsider.

943
00:38:05,440 --> 00:38:06,840
I really can't help you.

944
00:38:07,000 --> 00:38:09,560
We academics and you lawyers

945
00:38:09,560 --> 00:38:10,840
don't speak the same language.

946
00:38:10,840 --> 00:38:13,440
You'd better find someone else.

947
00:38:18,680 --> 00:38:19,320
Class monitor.

948
00:38:19,320 --> 00:38:20,720
Have some tea. Thank you.

949
00:38:24,320 --> 00:38:25,200
I'm sorry, Longnv.

950
00:38:25,200 --> 00:38:27,120
I couldn't be of much help to you.

951
00:38:29,200 --> 00:38:30,200
What did you call her?

952
00:38:30,200 --> 00:38:31,000
Longnv.

953
00:38:31,440 --> 00:38:33,200
Sounds like she has a physical defect.

954
00:38:33,200 --> 00:38:34,000
If you call her that,

955
00:38:34,000 --> 00:38:35,360
you have to call me Beihu.

956
00:38:35,360 --> 00:38:37,240
Of course, Beihu.

957
00:38:37,320 --> 00:38:39,450
Otherwise, should I call you Dongbei?

958
00:38:40,640 --> 00:38:42,370
You're so funny, Squad Leader.

959
00:38:42,520 --> 00:38:43,880
No, what are you doing?

960
00:38:43,880 --> 00:38:45,160
Acting like an idiot.

961
00:38:45,320 --> 00:38:46,720
No, I'm just trying to liven things up.

962
00:38:46,720 --> 00:38:48,480
Do we need you for that? Get out.

963
00:38:49,040 --> 00:38:50,100
Fine, I'll get out.

964
00:38:53,480 --> 00:38:54,440
I'm sorry.

965
00:38:54,440 --> 00:38:56,320
This kid is quite lively.

966
00:38:58,000 --> 00:38:59,720
Squad Leader, why

967
00:38:59,720 --> 00:39:01,980
is Director Zhuge unwilling to testify?

968
00:39:02,440 --> 00:39:03,720
Actually, Director Zhuge

969
00:39:03,720 --> 00:39:05,880
testified for me once a few years ago.

970
00:39:05,880 --> 00:39:06,880
But that time,

971
00:39:06,880 --> 00:39:08,320
the judge stated that psychotherapy

972
00:39:08,320 --> 00:39:10,160
is highly subjective,

973
00:39:10,160 --> 00:39:11,520
and ruled against us.

974
00:39:14,120 --> 00:39:15,760
So the old man cares a lot about his pride.

975
00:39:15,760 --> 00:39:17,120
If he won't do it, let's just find another expert.

976
00:39:17,120 --> 00:39:18,980
Is he the only one in the province?

977
00:39:19,720 --> 00:39:21,440
I'll just get out.

978
00:39:21,440 --> 00:39:22,170
Understood.

979
00:39:24,720 --> 00:39:25,560
You know what,

980
00:39:25,920 --> 00:39:28,440
he really is the only one authoritative enough.

981
00:39:28,440 --> 00:39:30,480
What if I write him a heartfelt letter

982
00:39:30,480 --> 00:39:32,540
to appeal to his emotions and reason?

983
00:39:32,880 --> 00:39:33,560
Sure.

984
00:39:34,000 --> 00:39:35,460
I'll talk to him again too.

985
00:39:35,720 --> 00:39:36,250
Hurry up.

986
00:39:39,520 --> 00:39:41,560
Do you two want to earn some credit?

987
00:39:44,000 --> 00:39:44,920
How?

988
00:39:51,400 --> 00:39:52,400
Is it this old man?

989
00:39:52,480 --> 00:39:53,140
Hello, sir.

990
00:39:53,240 --> 00:39:53,880
Hello.

991
00:39:54,720 --> 00:39:55,160
Yes.

992
00:39:55,800 --> 00:39:57,160
Come down and take a look.

993
00:39:57,160 --> 00:39:57,680
Hello.

994
00:39:58,320 --> 00:39:59,440
What are you doing?

995
00:39:59,800 --> 00:40:00,320
Where are you going?

996
00:40:00,320 --> 00:40:02,040
What are you doing? Are you going to hit him?

997
00:40:02,040 --> 00:40:04,080
Aren't we here to beg Professor Zhuge?

998
00:40:04,080 --> 00:40:05,880
How are you going to beg? Are you going to kneel down?

999
00:40:05,880 --> 00:40:06,520
Okay.

1000
00:40:06,520 --> 00:40:07,720
What do you mean, okay?

1001
00:40:07,720 --> 00:40:09,640
You can't ask for a favor empty-handed.

1002
00:40:09,640 --> 00:40:10,440
Just keep an eye on him for now.

1003
00:40:10,440 --> 00:40:11,500
I have my own plans.

1004
00:40:13,680 --> 00:40:15,440
Act natural. Come on, get up.

1005
00:40:18,160 --> 00:40:19,090
Is this natural?

1006
00:40:32,520 --> 00:40:33,680
What kind of level is this?

1007
00:40:33,680 --> 00:40:35,140
I can't catch a single one.

1008
00:40:36,360 --> 00:40:37,220
How about this?

1009
00:40:37,440 --> 00:40:39,840
You two find a place nearby and buy two fish.

1010
00:40:41,320 --> 00:40:42,320
Why buy fish?

1011
00:40:42,680 --> 00:40:44,440
Just go when I tell you to. Don't ask.

1012
00:40:44,440 --> 00:40:46,800
This can't be reimbursed. You have to pay for it yourself.

1013
00:40:46,800 --> 00:40:48,120
Fine, I'll pay for it.

1014
00:40:48,200 --> 00:40:49,200
Then I'll have a chat with your Sister Long

1015
00:40:49,200 --> 00:40:50,960
about you still being in Honghu.

1016
00:40:50,960 --> 00:40:52,480
Why are you like this?

1017
00:40:52,480 --> 00:40:53,120
Fine.

1018
00:40:53,320 --> 00:40:54,180
Hurry up and go.

1019
00:40:54,880 --> 00:40:55,800
There won't be any fresh ones left soon.

1020
00:40:55,800 --> 00:40:56,800
Hurry, hurry up.

1021
00:40:57,840 --> 00:40:58,640
Let's go.

1022
00:41:08,360 --> 00:41:09,640
Sir, I've been watching you all morning.

1023
00:41:09,640 --> 00:41:10,920
You haven't caught much.

1024
00:41:10,920 --> 00:41:13,000
There are just fewer fish this season.

1025
00:41:13,000 --> 00:41:15,200
What season? Are the fish hibernating?

1026
00:41:15,560 --> 00:41:17,360
You just picked the wrong spot.

1027
00:41:17,920 --> 00:41:19,120
I was just over there.

1028
00:41:19,360 --> 00:41:20,480
There were so many fish.

1029
00:41:20,480 --> 00:41:21,520
You don't even need to fish.

1030
00:41:21,520 --> 00:41:23,440
They were just jumping onto the shore.

1031
00:41:23,440 --> 00:41:24,920
Why don't you go fish over there?

1032
00:41:24,920 --> 00:41:25,760
You mean over there?

1033
00:41:25,760 --> 00:41:26,480
Yeah.

1034
00:41:26,640 --> 00:41:28,240
Come on, I'll take you there.

1035
00:41:28,400 --> 00:41:30,000
Come on, pack up your things.

1036
00:41:32,240 --> 00:41:32,720
I'll give it a try.

1037
00:41:32,720 --> 00:41:33,280
Yeah.

1038
00:41:39,240 --> 00:41:39,840
Bought it.

1039
00:41:40,280 --> 00:41:41,000
No problem.

1040
00:42:03,680 --> 00:42:05,040
Here it comes.

1041
00:42:05,080 --> 00:42:05,880
Got it. It took the bait.

1042
00:42:05,880 --> 00:42:07,000
Come, let me net it.

1043
00:42:07,000 --> 00:42:07,280
Don't rush.

1044
00:42:07,280 --> 00:42:08,600
Tire it out.

1045
00:42:08,640 --> 00:42:09,170
Alright.

1046
00:42:09,400 --> 00:42:10,360
Here it comes.

1047
00:42:10,360 --> 00:42:12,090
It's really big. Here it comes.

1048
00:42:13,160 --> 00:42:15,020
Your skills are really good, sir.

1049
00:42:15,720 --> 00:42:17,000
It's such a big one.

1050
00:42:17,080 --> 00:42:18,080
He's really good at this, right?

1051
00:42:18,080 --> 00:42:19,400
You guys are amazing.

1052
00:42:19,520 --> 00:42:20,120
Young man.

1053
00:42:20,520 --> 00:42:21,400
You're really something.

1054
00:42:21,400 --> 00:42:23,000
Just average. Very average.

1055
00:42:24,080 --> 00:42:25,280
How can it be average?

1056
00:42:26,040 --> 00:42:28,570
It's my first time catching a koi in the river.

1057
00:42:33,320 --> 00:42:34,720
Your first time?

1058
00:42:35,560 --> 00:42:37,360
I catch koi all the time.

1059
00:42:37,680 --> 00:42:39,080
Isn't there a saying?

1060
00:42:39,080 --> 00:42:40,080
It goes like this.

1061
00:42:40,600 --> 00:42:43,480
When koi arrives, great wealth and good luck naturally follow.

1062
00:42:43,480 --> 00:42:43,880
Right?

1063
00:42:44,800 --> 00:42:45,960
This young man really knows how to talk.

1064
00:42:45,960 --> 00:42:47,680
The God of Wealth is here. The God of Wealth is here.

1065
00:42:47,680 --> 00:42:49,320
Good deeds get good rewards.

1066
00:42:49,320 --> 00:42:51,240
The God of Wealth says to make money the right way.

1067
00:42:51,240 --> 00:42:52,240
Okay, okay, okay.

1068
00:42:52,600 --> 00:42:53,400
Stop acting.

1069
00:42:53,880 --> 00:42:56,680
You're from Lawyer Xiao's law firm, right?
